# The dev dashboard's production build (`vite build`; `build:e2e` and `vite dev` use other modes and
# never read this file, and `build:staging` reads .env.staging over it). admin.jackioh.com, behind
# Cloudflare Access (apps/admin/README.md).
#
# EVERY VALUE HERE IS PUBLIC. Vite compiles VITE_ values into the bundle every visitor downloads, the
# build writes the Supabase host into the CSP (public/_headers, headers.ts), and a Supabase publishable
# key is made to ship to browsers. Never put SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY, DATABASE_URL, CODE_PEPPER or anything
# else from crates/server/.env here: src/env.test.ts fails on any key but these two, on a secret-shaped
# value, and on a value apps/web/.env.production does not hold too.
#
# Supabase: production's own project, JackiOh-Production (docs/deploy-cloudflare.md section 8), the one
# the site's server (wrangler.jsonc's SUPABASE_URL) checks every sign-in against.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://fuzpvmjdejvbjcarypyi.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_Wrsaw5gK4Gf_Hts0-B1skQ_DfUUUv9i
